															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-a" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(226026); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=226026&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609387651" alt="Captain A" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=226026)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-a" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(226026); return false;" >Captain A</a></span> <span class="odate time_1239124762 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Apr 2009 17:19</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-442429">
									

<p>Illuminati is a great game, but the scale is much larger. The foundation could be a part of it, a "violent" group probably.</p>
<p>XK class missions defenitly need to be in the game. However, they do not need a precise rule : if a XK class mission is drawed, weel, good luck completing it, the reward will be great (maybe winning the game), but if you fail…everybody lose ^^^.<br />
Magis is simple by its mecanism : you play card, tap them and read text, that's it. Even "keywords" are useless, as most the meaning of them is on the card too. Magic is all about reading and patching combos : no strategy, no effort of memory, or luck, or wit. All you need is a good (= expensive and fresh new Type 2) deck to win ! That's why I stopped playing. BTW, VTES is born from R.Garfield too (what a guy).<br />
What we must achieve with this game is the exact opposite : using very simple card through complex mecanism to allow the players a infinite number of playing style, so they can never play two similar games. Playing TCG will only require to know the rules, not the cards. WINNING will require a coherent deck (no "682+176+clef rush deck"), observation skills, anticipation, a bit of luck and bluff and reason. Sometime you'll have to wait for the good time to move, sometime you'll strike your opponent here to scary him so he'll forget to do this, etc…</p>
<p>To make this go further, we'll need to start working on a precise set of card to test it. We do not need a lot :<br />
-15 missions (10+5 XK)<br />
-24 Thing cards (5 SCPs, 5 items, 5 people, 5 bases, 5 events (like spells, not staying in game, cheap/free)<br />
And that's it. As we used to say back in school "To do something, you need something to do".</p>

							</div>

								
					
