<p>I know you guys love Magic the Gathering but pleeaaase, we must not sacrifice the great universe of the Foundation in the name of accessibility and simplicity. This is not a PG13 game, not Yu Gi Oh, and mature, adult players are old enough to comprehend and use complex rules. Moreover, we definitly do not need to make it friendly/sellable.<br />
Moley's example of game is aberrant, cards are too expensive. As i said, this is all about balancing cards. Magic failed at this, furnishing a gigantic number of totaly useless cards, what we do not find in VTES (any card have it's utility and you can build a deck around it). Our priorities must be :<br />
-sticking to the creepy, violent and realistic universe<br />
-"secure" "contain" and "protect" mecanisms<br />
-place the player in a position where he have to handle limited ressources and risky weapons<br />
-stregth through sacrifice, success through deceive<br />
What we must not do is<br />
-"i attack you/i play spell/your turn" mecanism<br />
-"i won/you lose" endings<br />
-"biggest numbers are the best"<br />
Still, let see Gears proposal before anything.</p>

							</div>

								
					
