				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/moley" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301944); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=301944&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609387651" alt="Moley" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=301944)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/moley" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301944); return false;" >Moley</a></span> <span class="odate time_1239290826 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Apr 2009 15:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-444626">
									

<p>Complexity rocks, I agree but you don't want to end up like the Decipher version of Star Wars, or even VTES at times, where there are so many rule exception cards and escapes it ends up sounding like the geriatric version of YGO.</p>
<p>As Clef perfectly put it emergent complexity is the way to go in my opinion. Rules for the sake of complexity means the game will die. Even if you don't want to sell it and want to just keep it on site if new members feel like the game is designed for the people who've been here a while to play they'll shy away from it.</p>
<p>The idea of using any card as a resource is a good one, it solves the fundimental "mana screw/glut" problems that many CCGs suffer from and allows for players to make desisions on whats important NOW compare to what can let them win later.</p>
<p>The idea that missions and SCPs are a universal goal, so while you can put the mission and SCP on the table your opponent could just finish it before you and mooch the victory would add the risk you've been looking for without bogging the game down with endless exceptions.</p>
<p>I understand you don't want to make a game you see as "kiddy" but just slapping on complexity isn't the way to go about it and not using terms and effects because they sound too YuGiOh will just hamper the development even more.</p>
<p>…wow I sound like a cock when I make these posts don't I?</p>

							</div>

								
					
